    "leafs": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Maple Leafs",
      "league": "NHL",
      "record": "32-36-14",
      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season didn't merely sputter out - it fell off a cliff, leaving Toronto with a <strong>32-36-14</strong> mark, <strong>78 points</strong>, and an <strong>8th-place finish in the Atlantic Division</strong> after a <strong>L7</strong> tailspin that sealed a <strong>15th-overall</strong> position and a spring without a pulse. <strong>Auston Matthews still wants to win in Toronto, the GM says</strong> - and that is the franchise's first and loudest mandate now, because the Maple Leafs cannot keep pretending patience will cure a roster that never found enough bite, enough backbone, or enough depth to survive the grind. The headlines from the scouting combine tell you where this is headed: draft, prospects, trade buzz, all the usual machinery of a club that has run out of excuses and must decide whether to tweak, retool, or dare something bigger. The one thing that cannot change is the ask on Matthews and the core around him; when the captain's desire remains real, the organization's duty is to match it with competence. <strong>Watch the coaching decision, the July shopping list, and whether Toronto finally uses the draft and cap space to build a harder, younger team</strong>.",
        "updated": "Updated June 11, 2026"
      },
